WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
-My next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.305
whose stand-up special
"Brian Regan on the Rocks"

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.106
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.242
Here is Brian Regan!

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:11.945
Wow! That's what I'm talking --

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.246
Look at you.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.348
Wow.
-Hey, Jimmy, how are you?

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.249
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:19.618
Brian, you know
I'm a big fan of yours,

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.621
but I -- Something's different.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.356
You look a little different.
Is it --

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.858
It's the hair. Is that new hair?

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.362
-You guys were talking about it
earlier with Luke Bryan

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.031
and about -- You know,
it's the gray hair thing.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.666
I don't know what happened
either, Jimmy.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.334
-New hair.
-COVID hit.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.036
-Yeah.
-I went into hibernation,

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.838
and I came out a senior citizen.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.407
-[ Laughs ] Wow. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:45.345
-I looked down, I was like,
"Hey, is that an AARP card?"

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.445
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.081
You did it! You made it.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.582
-Yeah.
-I know that you've been

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.852
back on the road,
which is awesome,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.521
as crowds are kind of
coming out again slowly,

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.189
and you've been traveling.

00:00:57.189 --> 00:01:01.060
What is it like
flying these days?

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.261
-I don't know, man.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:05.798
I just always think
weird things, you know.

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:08.767
You know when the plane
backs away from the gate?

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.703
-Yeah, sure.
-Just once,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.706
I want the pilot
to pop open the door

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.142
and say, "Hey, put your heads
down, I'm backing up."

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.643
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.279
-"Yeah, you know how hard it is
to pull back this thing?"

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.382
-"Yeah, get your heads down.
I'm trying to back up here.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:25.218
18C, what's the matter with you?
Get your head down."

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.952
The guy's --

00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:29.055
-What does Brian Regan do?

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.558
Are you a window seat guy,
or are you an aisle seat?

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:35.828
-Well, I --
I'd like to get an aisle.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.831
I'll I try to get an emergency
exit row seat if I can do that.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.500
-Absolutely, yeah.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.302
-Yeah. You know
what kills me, though?

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.770
When you're in
the emergency exit row seat,

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.207
and you agree to save everyone,

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:52.412
how come when the flight
is over, no one thanks you?

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:55.347
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:58.250
Pretty amazing. Pretty amazing
what you might have done,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.920
you know? You think someone
would take note of it

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.022
on the way out, you know?
A little pat on back,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:06.959
"Hey, I heard what went down
before takeoff.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.729
Unbelievable.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.165
The fact that you were willing
to put your life on the line

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:17.704
to save me, my family, and all
the other souls on this plane

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:21.174
is one of the greatest gifts
a human can offer to another.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.609
Thank you
from the bottom of my heart."

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.311
No, nothing.
-Nothing at all.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.714
-Just a backpack, a backpack
to the back of the head.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:31.718
"Hey, I was
an almost-responder!"

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:36.122
-[ Laughs ] An almost-responder.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.757
When you do get to your gigs,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.394
do you have a driver,
or do you rent a car?

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.096
-[ Chuckles ] I have a driver,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.998
He's called Brian.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.333
-Oh, okay. Wow, yeah,
I didn't know.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.637
-Yeah, I get -- I try to get
a rental car every now and then.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:54.440
And in fact,
I had to cancel one recently.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.509
And I called, and the guy said,

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.278
"Well, you're calling
within 24 hours,

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.014
so we need to charge you
for a day."

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.115
And I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.551
And I was like, "Hey,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.920
am I allowed to change
the reservation?"

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.355
And he goes, "Yeah, I guess."

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.656
I said, "Alright.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:15.861
I just realized I need
to pick it up 48 hours from now.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.697
Yeah? Can you change it
officially in the computer?

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:20.532
Is it official? Yeah?

00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:21.934
I want to cancel it."

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.436
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.071
-That's the way to do it, man.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.705
That's the way to do it, bud.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.808
I want to talk the you about --
'Cause I know

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.742
you got your special on Netflix
"On the Rocks,"

00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:32.110
but then you're on the --

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.947
You're part of the cast
of the show "Loudermilk"...

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.450
-Yes.
-that is fantastic, by the way.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.618
-Thank you.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.052
-And you're doing
some serious acting in this.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.320
You got some chops, buddy.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.755
-Well, I'm honored to be in it.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.558
It's called "Loudermilk."
It's on Prime Video.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.792
It's a dark comedy.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:50.330
Peter Farrelly and Bobby Mort
co-created it.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.365
Third season just came out.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.501
Ron Livingston plays Loudermilk,

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.436
who runs
a substance abuse group,

00:03:57.436 --> 00:04:00.873
and he's got a bunch of misfits
in the group,

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.810
and I fit in there perfectly.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.146
And it's fun to be in, man.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.717
Peter Farrelly saw me perform

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:15.120
at a comedy festival called
LucyFest, and he came up to me

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.223
and said that he was doing
this "Loudermilk" thing

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.991
and wanted to know
if I wanted to be in it.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.026
So I'm honored that
he put me in this thing.

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:23.762
-Yeah, he actually
just was quoted somewhere

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:25.098
saying that this season,

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.567
you have some of the best acting
on television,

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.668
and that's Peter Farrelly,
who has won an Oscar,

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.170
I just want to remind everyone.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.405
Not too shabby --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.373
Not too shabby, Brian Regan.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:35.875
-So he got my check.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.010
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.344
-I'm honored, man.

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:41.247
He's a great director.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.782
And he gave me some fun stuff
to do in Season 3.

00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:44.917
So I'm happy to be in it.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.186
-Yeah, this season,
you get really in there.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.521
I want to --
We're gonna show a clip.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:51.991
Would you like
to set up this clip?

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.394
-Well, I'm an alcoholic.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.896
I'm estranged from my family.
I'm estranged from my kids.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.464
I'm trying to reconnect --
-Brian, I'm talking about the --

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.099
I'm talking about the TV show.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.135
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:06.239
-Okay. Let's get back on that.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.742
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.978
I'm not acting in the show.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.715
I'm just being me.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.752
So, anyway, one of my sons
asked me to go to career day

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:23.489
to talk about my job,
and I'm nervous as heck.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.359
I'm an exterminator.
When I get there, I find out

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.160
I have to follow a guy
who's a scientist

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.229
who just isolated a gene.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.730
I'm like,
"We don't need to do this.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.399
These kids have seen plenty."

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.800
And they're like, "No, no, no.
You're next."

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.570
So this is me trying to impress
my son and his friends.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.305
-That's awesome.
I want to show everyone.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:42.174
This is Brian Regan in the new
season of "Loudermilk."

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.509
Take a look at this.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.578
-Well, sometimes
parents don't want skunks

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:49.916
knocking on their door,
so they, uh -- they call me,

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.118
and I come over, and I --
and I kill it.

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:54.553
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.122
-You kill skunks?

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.024
-Yeah, yeah. I kill skunks.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:01.194
I kill possums. I kill rats.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.095
Anything with four legs or more,

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.666
I will come over to your house,
and I will kill it.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:07.867
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.102
So, are there any questions?

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.938
-What kind of person
kills animals for a living?

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:17.109
-That is an excellent question.
A licensed exterminator.

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:18.778
-You're a psychopath.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.446
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.648
-Brian Regan, everybody!

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:26.719
Watch all three seasons
of "Loudermilk" on Amazon Prime.

